  "scope_limits": [
    "Original publisher-hosted Rodríguez et al. (2020) PDF acquired; actual pages 6, 7 and 29–31 visually reviewed. Some PDF operations emitted color-space warnings; native Figure 2 RGB pixels were independently verified, and local current values come from readable text. Original source assets are not republished.",
    "The field study describes the northern post-split Quantum I component. No pre-split parent or Quantum II values are inherited; registry physical crosswalk remains unverified.",
    "Figure 2 explicitly dates the black current front 26 March 2018 and calls it model-inferred. Its eastern side is clipped. The 225–275 km interval measures the selected visible meridional extent only; it is not a full front extent, observed boundary, east–west width or eddy diameter.",
    "Eight latitude tick windows and four extremum windows were checked. The southern window excludes bottom-axis ticks. Six-pixel extent margins, two-pixel independent anchor shifts, two ink gates and outward 25 km rounding produce 512 reading scenarios; model/front error is unspecified. No geometry is reconstructed.",
    "At the local comparison, 26 March source speeds are about 0.8 m/s for the 5 m ADCP and a shared approximate 1.1 m/s for ROCIS/DopplerScatt; 25 March values are 0.6 and 1.2 m/s. Shared source approximations are not arithmetic averages or separately resolved independent estimates.",
    "Remote effective near-surface weighting has no single assigned depth. Roughly hour-scale instrument offsets do not establish a simultaneous depth section or a calculated shear. These local references are not means or whole-eddy maxima.",
    "The source longitude −95.55° and latitude wording in Figure 23/24 captions conflict with plotted longitude axes/context; no geometry is derived from those discrepancies. Generic LCE speeds, swath dimensions and cell-noise statistics are not assigned as individual eddy dimensions or observation-specific uncertainty.",
    "No physical footprint, state containment, seasonal envelope, runtime or release installation."
  ],
  "full_goal_complete": false
